  [PASS] 7A the sigma-binned eta_opt is neither flat nor unity: it rises monotonically with sigma across the whole optical range, so there is no clean step at sigma ~ 300 km/s and no 'no missing mass below 300' plateau here   (canonical median eta_opt over all 309 groups = 5.75 (alt 4.76); sigma bins ['75:1.35', '125:5.28', '175:11.00', '225:23.56', '275:38.85', '350:49.33', '650:196.45'])
  [PASS] 7A-bias AGAINST INTEREST (1) -- the sigma-binned form above is a BIASED estimator and must not be read as a measurement: sigma from 5-30 members carries 20-30% noise and eta goes as sigma^4, so E[eta] is inflated, and the inflation is worst in the low-sigma bins, which is the direction that would FAKE a step   (canonical sigma_obs/sigma_pred by luminosity bin = [1.387, 1.446, 1.553, 1.741, 2.65] (eta = [3.7, 4.37, 5.82, 9.18, 49.33]); alt = [1.323, 1.38, 1.482, 1.661, 2.528])
  [PASS] 7A-bias AGAINST INTEREST (2) -- and the subsample IS dispersion-selected.  The catalogue carries its own dynamical mass (from sigma and R_g) and its own luminosity mass; in the whole catalogue the two agree in the median, but in the Nm >= 5, sigma > 0 subsample used here the dynamical mass runs HIGH.  That is a selection on sigma at fixed luminosity, and it inflates eta_opt directly   (median M_dyn/M_lum = 0.66 in this subsample vs 0.15 in the whole catalogue (1536 groups with both) -- a factor 4.42)
  third reason not to read branch A as a measurement: KT2017 assigns membership out to the SECOND TURNAROUND
  radius R2t, so sigma is measured over infalling, non-virialised material, while the deep-MOND virial theorem
  applies to a bound, relaxed, isolated system.  The published MOND group analyses (Milgrom 2018, 2019) select
  relaxed groups precisely to avoid this.  Branch A is therefore recorded as CONTAMINATED, not as a null and
  not as a liability; branch B is the one that carries the item.
  sensitivity: Upsilon_K = 0.8 gives median eta_opt = 4.31 (vs 5.75 at 0.6)
  sensitivity: Upsilon_K = 1.0 gives median eta_opt = 3.45 (vs 5.75 at 0.6)
  the LambdaCDM-side comparison from the same catalogue: NEWTONIAN virial mass / stellar mass has median 52 -- Newtonian dynamics needs ~2 orders of magnitude of dark matter in these same groups where the framework needs a factor of a few.
  [PASS] M7A mutation: tripling a_0 must move eta_opt by exactly a factor 3 (it enters linearly) and does   (median eta with 3 a_0 = 1.92 vs 5.75)

